# Edgar, King of Figaro's Two-Headed Coin: "The first time you flip one or more coins each turn, those coins come up heads and
# you win those flips" (CR 705.3). Every die the script fixes is face 2, a lost flip. Turn 3: Bot1's Mana Crypt flips in its
# upkeep, the first flip of the turn, so Bot1 wins it whatever the coin shows (the ruling) and takes no damage; The Gold
# Saucer's flip later that turn is the second, so it is lost and makes no Treasure. Turn 4: Bot2's own Mana Crypt flip is
# not Bot1's, and Bot2 loses it (3 damage). Turn 5: a new turn, and Bot1's Mana Crypt flip is won again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mana Crypt
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Edgar, King of Figaro
The Gold Saucer
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mana Crypt
Island x23

[Dice]
2; 2; 2; 2; 2

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Crypt.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Edgar, King of Figaro.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.The Gold Saucer.Play

[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot2.Pass

[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Crypt.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.The Gold Saucer.Activate(Ability: #2)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5

[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Life = 17

[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
